virtio-win guest drivers for Windows, imported from upstream
============================================================

Upstream:  https://github.com/virtio-win/kvm-guest-drivers-windows
Tag:       mm324
Commit:    b1a462514ad70f30e5f2df4bd8e5cdc4b40193f5 (2026-09-14)
License:   BSD-3-Clause (LICENSE in this directory and in each subdirectory)
Authors:   Red Hat, Inc. and the other copyright holders named in LICENSE
           and in the file headers

Imported subset, unmodified at import time:
- LICENSE
- VirtIO/          VirtIO PCI and ring library, and its KMDF layer (VirtIO/WDF)
- Balloon/sys/     memory balloon driver (KMDF)

Not imported: Visual Studio project and solution files, .props files, batch
scripts and .clang-format. Changes made for the ReactOS build are listed below.

ReactOS changes
---------------
The ReactOS build uses GCC on case-sensitive file systems and does not run
the WPP trace preprocessor. These changes adapt the code to that. The code
paths are unchanged; only how the drivers report traces differs:

- Include file names match the files' case ("VirtIO.h", <ntddk.h>) and use
  forward slashes.
- VirtIO/osdep.h defines "inline" as __forceinline only for MSVC, and
  VirtIO/linux/types.h defines __attribute__ away only for compilers other
  than GCC, because GCC needs both as they are.
- VirtIO/kdebugprint.h and Balloon/sys/trace.h use ##__VA_ARGS__, so a
  message without arguments compiles with GCC.
- Balloon/sys/trace.h does not define EVENT_TRACING (WPP) for ReactOS; the
  driver prints through DbgPrintEx instead, and Balloon/sys/utils.c limits
  the driver's own traces to warnings and errors, because every message
  reaches the debugger and the interrupt and DPC traces would flood it.
  The VirtIO library's DPrintf messages up to level 4 still print, at
  device start.
- Callback functions that KMDF or the kernel call through a typed pointer
  are declared NTAPI. The WDK compiles x86 drivers with __stdcall as the
  default convention (/Gz); GCC defaults to __cdecl.
- Inline functions defined in headers (Balloon/sys/ProtoTypes.h,
  VirtIO/virtio_pci.h) are static, since GCC's C99 inline semantics differ
  from MSVC's. In VirtIO/WDF/Dma.c, "static FORCEINLINE" became
  "static __inline", because FORCEINLINE expands to "extern inline" with
  GCC in ReactOS.
- Balloon/sys/memstat.c no longer pastes "." with a field name in a macro.

Fixes
-----
Defects of the upstream code fixed here (to be offered upstream):

- Balloon: the device takes 32-bit page frame numbers, but on 64-bit
  Windows the driver sent its native 64-bit PFN_NUMBER array, so the host
  read every second entry as frame 0 and released guest page 0 once per
  ballooned page. The driver now sends a 32-bit array, sized one page as
  before (1024 frames per batch on both architectures), and allocates only
  pages whose frame numbers fit in 32 bits.
